y hour okay friday came in  the same thing we were like okay let's  still wait to see  if something was gonna happen but then  the intention was increasing  literally like i'm not like we literally  could not eat we literally could not  sleep like there was no peace like no  rest at all even shot in our eyes was  like a wrist because we didn't know what  was going to happen  so saturday morning  because zaparoja is just one hour one  hour applause to the nip danny pro so we  started hearing from zappos that the  russians were trying to evade we're  gonna evade soon and people in denial of  other people in their neighborhood like  they were leaving and all that so i live  with two other people um two other  friends  right i have two other roommates over  three so we're like okay we cannot stay  we have to leave because everybody's  leaving and then from if the russians  when the russians invade zap before you  know what they're going to come into  denibro and then we can't stay so that  was wrong we decided that we were going  to leave  okay we decided that we're going to  leave yeah  right you made it to to hungary  eventually  how did you make it there  we had to struggle our way through it  all  like  we have to struggle our way through it  all  all right so  when the initial plan was actually to go  to poland  was going to go to poland but then  when we went to the train station at  denipro train station there were a whole  lot of people who like the place was  full  so  they weren't sending tickets to us first  of all they went inside to get to us  blacks  they said you have to enter with tickets  the winner selling tickets to us they  were only selling this guess to  ukrainians  all right so we thought we we thought  okay what what can we do we have to  leave we can't stay so eventually we're  gonna have to push our way through all  right the train came the train came  with our lords  it was like we're just going up and down  because they were telling me telling us  that it was it was here it was there so  like it was a struggle we're just going  up and down up and down finally go to  the train finally got to the train you  know they said that we couldn't enter  that we couldn't enter because we didn't  have tickets and we're telling them that  you guys would not allow us to you guys  will not sell tickets to us i know  you're telling us that we cannot enter  because we don't have tickets so there  were a lot of guys a lot of african  african guys black guys so they were  trying to push their way in but you know  that these people this the police  literally went inside the train to bring  them out like bring them all out but the  ones that could fight their way like  fight their way  and fought their way inside deep inside  so they couldn't go deep inside but the  one that couldn't go deep inside the  train they literally went inside to  bring them back to bring them outside  and we we girls i literally because i  like me and my roommate crushes the girl  we fell down because of the struggle and  everything so we couldn't get on that  train so when the train finally came and  the train was coming from zapposia  because where our friends you know we're  on the train so they were able to also  keep seats for us  and help us so that was how we had a  struggle like we had a fight we had to  literally struggle and fight to enter  inside that trade even as much as we  should enter the train there was nowhere  to sit down there was nowhere to see  that like literally people were standing  people were  sleeping on the on the bypass i don't  know if you end up drinking not the  bypass who was sleeping there who were  sitting there and all but because our  friends you know kept it for us from zap  so that was how i was able to i were  able to push through push through to go  meet our friends where we where we um  where they were and that was how we were  able to manage to sit down because  obviously there was no space to lie down  we had to sit down and the trip the  journey from denipro to leave was like  18 hours in the dream 18 hours after all  the struggle we hadn't we had not eaten  we hadn't slept 18 hours you're in a  safer place right now  um what's next for you  what's next for me like it's literally  really complicated because now the eu  from our um from the news yesterday now  the er is saying that they can't  accommodate us students that they are  only acting as a pass by where students  can compass and go back to their country  so it's really really complicated for us  so we're trying to see within the short  period of  two weeks that we have which school is  going to accept us because we can't even  get our transcripts because of what is  happening in ukraine we don't have our  transcript but they don't seem to  understand that we don't have  transcripts we don't have transcripts so  like the like so it's it's it's really  really complicated for us like  the next step is really really  complicated for us you know  so uncertainty about the future uh well  um  thank you for speaking to us and we hope  that you're able to find a way forward  for the future  thank you so much
 

